1
00:00:00,175 --> 00:00:04,104
Pull a metal spring twice as far—and it pulls back twice as hard.

2
00:00:04,575 --> 00:00:06,845
A scrambled riddle? Prove your hidden law!

3
00:00:07,125 --> 00:00:09,268
As the stretch, so the force—F equals minus k x!

4
00:00:09,625 --> 00:00:14,983
With his brass microscope, Robert Hooke peered into cork—and named its honeycomb rooms 'cells'!

5
00:00:15,625 --> 00:00:18,222
Push a spring past its elastic limit—and it snaps forever.

6
00:00:18,625 --> 00:00:20,061
Hey—that ruined my watch!

7
00:00:20,625 --> 00:00:24,996
Tame that tiny hairspring inside a balance wheel—and humanity mastered portable time.

8
00:00:25,625 --> 00:00:29,282
Car suspensions, skyscrapers, even DNA strands today? Still obeying Hooke's law.
